From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:14:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/11] vulkan: fuse RMS_NORM + SCALE

A SCALE without bias that follows an RMS_NORM rides in the norm's unused
param2, so the pair is one launch. Qwen3-Coder-Next issues 72 such pairs
a generated token (the q/k norms of its linear-attention layers); Metal
fuses them too. A SCALE with a bias, or by 0 (param2's "none"), is left
alone.

test-backend-ops: RMS_NORM_SCALE cases at the model's shape and with a
bias and a zero scale; the existing RMS_NORM_SCALE, RMS_NORM, ADD_RMS_NORM
and RMS_NORM_MUL_* cases pass.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h      |  1 +
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp          | 29 ++++++++++++-
 .../ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/rms_norm.comp  |  3 +-
 .../vulkan-shaders/rms_norm_partials.comp     |  3 +-
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp                    | 43 +++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h
index 88d0f3a37..7b43adc11 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h
